msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:22
#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:24
msgid "\"{}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:30
msgid "“The implementation only uses safe Rust."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:32
msgid "What can we learn from this?"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:34
msgid ""
"“It is impossible for `copy` to trigger memory safety issues when "
"implemented in Safe Rust. This is true for all possible input arguments.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:37
msgid ""
"“For example, by using Rust’s iterators, we can ensure that we’ll never "
"trigger errors relating to handling pointers directly, such as needing null "
"pointer or bounds checks.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:41
msgid "Ask: “Can you think of any others?”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:43
msgid "No aliasing issues"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:44
msgid "Dangling pointers are impossible"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:45
msgid "Alignment will be correct"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:46
msgid "Cannot accidentally read from uninitialized memory"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:48
msgid ""
"“We can say that the `copy` function is _sound_ because Rust ensures that "
"all of the safety preconditions are satisfied.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:51
msgid ""
"“From the point of view of the programmer, as this function is implemented "
"in safe Rust, we can think of it as having no safety preconditions.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/safe.md:54
msgid ""
"“This does not mean that `copy` will always do what the caller might want. "
"If there is insufficient space available in the `dest` slice, then data will "
"not be copied across.”"
msgstr ""
